This breaks static methods. For whatever reason their `is_valid()` returns false, but their Object is the source GDScript. Example:
```GDScript
@tool
extends EditorScript

class CustomNode extends Node:
	static func test():
		print(1)

func _run():
	var tw = Engine.get_main_loop().create_tween()
	tw.tween_callback(CustomNode.test)
```
Does not work with this PR.

> I think custom callables will never return `true` from `is_null()`. My understanding is that `is_null` is a completely empty callable

Yeah, I think that's the desired behavior, but if you look at the implementation of `Callable::is_null()`:

```c++
	_FORCE_INLINE_ bool is_null() const {
		return method == StringName() && object == 0;
	}
```

I think a callable created via `callable_mp_static()` would have an empty `method` and `object`, and so return `true` from `is_null()`. Although, I haven't tested it yet, I'm just reading through the code.
